;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljk:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved
;; (authoring fetch: 2026-08-22, GLEIF golden copy publishDate 2026-08-22).
;;
;; FOUR independent sources are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system (the entity record, its ISIN mapping, its
;;     direct-children page, both parent reporting exceptions, the RA000602
;;     entry in the registration-authorities registry, the XTIQ entry in the
;;     entity-legal-forms registry, the LEI record and issuer record of the
;;     managing LOU, and the SEPARATE LEI record of the operating subsidiary
;;     whose name appears on the archived Terms of Use -- see below)
;;   * the United States, via the SEC's EDGAR submissions API, the company-tickers
;;     file, the XBRL companyfacts API, and the inline-XBRL cover page of the
;;     FY2025 Form 10-K (the NYSE filer, CIK 0001437578, a large accelerated
;;     filer -- 10-K, 10-Q, 8-K, DEF 14A)
;;   * the State of Delaware, via the Division of Corporations portal at
;;     corp.delaware.gov -- the very register RA000602 names (portal only; see
;;     below for why no per-entity row exists)
;;   * the issuer itself, at its corporate home page (schema.org Corporation
;;     block) and at the exact Terms-of-Use page this repository archives in
;;     80-data/public/tos.journal.edn
;;
;; A YOUNG LEI ON A 2008 ENTITY. GLEIF issued this LEI on 2025-12-10 (row
;; gleif-initial-registration) -- the record is eight months old at authoring
;; and has never been renewed (row gleif-next-renewal). The ENTITY is older:
;; GLEIF's creationDate is 2008-05-09 (row gleif-creation-date). EDGAR agrees
;; from the other side without quoting GLEIF: the filer's one formerName is
;; BRIGHT HORIZONS SOLUTIONS CORP with a 2008-06-11 date (row
;; sec-former-name-2008), and the 10-K narrates the same year -- "listed on
;; Nasdaq from 1998 to May 2008 when we were acquired and went private" (row
;; sec-10k-went-private-2008), then the 2013-01-30 IPO onto the NYSE under BFAM
;; (row sec-10k-ipo-nyse). The 2008 corporation that holds this LEI is the
;; going-private vehicle, not the 1986 founding company.
;;
;; HOW GLEIF AND DELAWARE ARE LINKED -- BY SHARED KEY, RESOLVED ONE WAY ONLY.
;; GLEIF names RA000602 (Division of Corporations, Department of State,
;; Delaware) as both register of record and validation authority, and records
;; registeredAs 4548355 and validatedAs 4548355 -- the Delaware file number
;; (rows gleif-registered-as, gleif-validated-as). The same digits reappear
;; inside GLEIF's OpenCorporates pointer ocid us_de/4548355 (row gleif-ocid).
;; Delaware exposes NO stable public per-entity URL: the ICIS entity search at
;; icis.corp.delaware.gov is form-gated. So the file number can be READ OUT of
;; GLEIF but not RESOLVED at the register itself by this gate -- the
;; corp.delaware.gov row is :definition (the register exists, and its own page
;; points at ICIS), not :identity (the register names this entity).
;;
;; HOW GLEIF AND THE SEC ARE LINKED -- BY ATTRIBUTES, NOT BY KEY. EDGAR carries
;; "lei":null for this filer (row sec-lei-null, which goes red the day EDGAR
;; starts printing the LEI, at which point a direct-key row should replace it).
;; EDGAR's submissions API ALSO carries stateOfIncorporation "" -- EMPTY (row
;; sec-state-of-inc-empty). The submissions API therefore cannot corroborate
;; GLEIF's jurisdiction US-DE. The 10-K cover page CAN: its inline-XBRL tag
;; dei:EntityIncorporationStateCountryCode reads Delaware (rows
;; sec-10k-inc-state-tag, sec-10k-inc-state-value). Two SEC surfaces, one of
;; them blank -- the catalog cites the one that answers and records that the
;; other does not. The remaining links are attributes in agreement: the exact
;; legal name (row sec-name), the EIN 80-0188269 printed both in the
;; submissions API without its hyphen (row sec-ein) and on the 10-K cover with
;; it (row sec-10k-ein), and the headquarters address below.
;;
;; ONE ADDRESS, THREE REGISTERS, AND A REGISTERED AGENT. GLEIF's headquarters
;; address is 2 Wells Avenue, Newton, US-MA 02459 (rows gleif-hq-*); EDGAR's
;; business AND mailing address is 2 WELLS AVENUE, NEWTON, MA 02459 (rows
;; sec-street, sec-city, sec-state, sec-zip); the 10-K cover tags the same
;; street (row sec-10k-address); the issuer's own home page carries it in a
;; schema.org Corporation block with legalName, locality, region, postal code
;; and telephone (rows issuer-home-*). GLEIF's LEGAL address is different and
;; is not the company: C/O CORPORATION SERVICE COMPANY, 251 LITTLE FALLS DRIVE,
;; WILMINGTON DE 19808 (rows gleif-legal-*) -- the registered agent CSC, an
;; address shared with a large share of Delaware registrants (the managing LOU
;; below uses the same agent). A reader who joins on GLEIF's legal address
;; joins on the agent, not on the company. blueprint.edn records jurisdiction
;; US-MA: that is where the company SITS (GLEIF hq region, EDGAR state), not
;; where it is INCORPORATED (GLEIF jurisdiction US-DE, 10-K cover Delaware).
;; Massachusetts' own foreign-corporation register (corp.sec.state.ma.us) is
;; form-gated, so no Massachusetts-register row exists.
;;
;; THE TERMS OF USE NAME A DIFFERENT LEGAL ENTITY. The archived page states
;; that its content "is owned or controlled by Bright Horizons Family Solutions
;; LLC" (row issuer-tos-llc-owner) -- the LLC, not the Inc. The LLC is a
;; separate legal person with its OWN LEI, 254900BHOU40CFNXWQ75, a Delaware
;; limited liability company (legal form HZEH) created 1998-04-27 with Delaware
;; file number 2888832, headquartered at the same 2 WELLS AVENUE and managed by
;; the same LOU (rows llc-gleif-*). The 10-K ties the two together in the
;; Inc.'s own words: "Bright Horizons Family Solutions LLC (the Borrower), the
;; Company's wholly-owned subsidiary" (row sec-10k-llc-subsidiary). GLEIF does
;; NOT tie them: the LLC's direct-parent reporting exception still reads NO_LEI
;; (row llc-gleif-parent-exception-no-lei) -- true when the LLC registered in
;; 2017, false since 2025-12-10 when the parent obtained this LEI -- and the
;; LLC record was last updated on 2026-08-21 without correcting it. GLEIF's
;; relationship graph therefore shows no edge between parent and subsidiary
;; even though both nodes exist; the edge is asserted by the SEC filing only.
;; That row goes red the day GLEIF records the relationship, which is the
;; correct outcome: a stale-exception row must not outlive the exception.
;;
;; WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CITED. GLEIF's ISIN mapping for this LEI is EMPTY
;; (row gleif-isin-empty, total 0) although the common stock trades on the
;; NYSE as BFAM; the ISIN is therefore not asserted here -- a ticker is not an
;; ISIN and GLEIF has not mapped one. The Inc. reports NO direct or ultimate
;; accounting-consolidation parent (reason NO_KNOWN_PERSON, rows
;; gleif-*-parent-exception) and GLEIF lists zero direct children (row
;; gleif-children-empty) -- the LLC above is not listed as a child for the
;; reason just given. nyse.com's quote page renders client-side and carries
;; the symbol only inside a script config, so it is not cited as a register.
;;
;; Rows carry :cite/row-kind so a reader can tell what each one proves:
;;   :identity   -- the register names THIS entity (key-bearing claim)
;;   :attribute  -- a fact about the entity, corroborating but not identifying
;;   :definition -- the register/code/authority exists and is what GLEIF says
;;
;; Run the gate:   nbb tools/verify_citations.cljk facts/catalog.edn --min 20

